  [0.04, -0.02, 0.02, 0.02, 0.02], 0.070, 0.078, 0.092, 0.020,
  "Founded in 1924 as Compagnie française des pétroles at the direction of the French government. Patrick Pouyanné has been CEO since 2014. TotalEnergies is the European major that committed most seriously to an integrated power strategy — it owns and operates a large renewable generation and electricity retail business alongside conventional oil and gas. Its LNG portfolio is second only to Shell's, and its upstream assets are spread across Africa, the Middle East, the North Sea and Brazil. It has significant exposure to Mozambique LNG, a project delayed for years by regional security problems.",
  [("Exploration & Production", 43), ("Integrated LNG", 24), ("Downstream & Chemicals", 22), ("Integrated Power", 11)],
  ["Integrated Power gives a credible energy transition strategy that most peers abandoned, and management now targets positive free cash flow in 2027 and a 12% return on capital by 2030.",
   "One of the highest dividend yields among the majors, and in September 2026 the board committed to growing the dividend by more than 5% a year through 2030.",
   "LNG position is strategically valuable in a Europe permanently reducing Russian gas dependence."],
  ["Mozambique LNG remains delayed and the capital deployed is not yet generating returns.",
   "African upstream assets carry political and security risk.",
   "European majors trade at persistent discounts and French tax policy is unpredictable."],
  "Favoured among European majors for the power strategy and yield. The September 2026 strategy update raised the fourth-quarter buyback to $2.5 billion from $1.5 billion and targeted 4% annual energy production growth to 2030, but the shares slipped and the debate remains whether renewables investment dilutes returns.",
  "Mozambique LNG construction progress, Integrated Power reaching positive free cash flow in 2027, quarterly buyback size, dividend policy, oil price.",
