  [0.14, 0.13, 0.11, 0.10, 0.09], 0.11, 0.19, 0.095, 0.028,
  "Spun out of General Electric in April 2024 to hold the energy businesses. Scott Strazik is CEO. GE Vernova makes gas turbines, in which it is one of only three credible global suppliers alongside Siemens Energy and Mitsubishi; grid equipment including high-voltage transformers and switchgear, which is in severe global shortage; and wind turbines, the weakest part of the portfolio. Data centre electricity demand has produced a gas turbine order backlog stretching years into the future, and the electrification segment has become the profit story.",
